41,2,2,talk,Yumi,,"- **Yumi**: @George, that’s a relief. If technicians have spare hours, maybe we can cover the gaps without new hires.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,George,,"@Yumi, don’t be too quick. Those spare hours are spent on manual checks the broken equipment forces us to do.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@George, that explains the discrepancy. My post-occupancy data shows high ratings only where booking is open, not where benefits stay internal.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Mizuki, open booking drives usage, but my reserve data shows we never budgeted to replace the kit. We’re borrowing from the future.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"- **Shizue**: @Benjamin, that is a heavy burden. My weather diaries confirm six weeks lost to rain, yet the tender records show plant costs rising sharply.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Yumi,,"@Benjamin, that’s a sobering thought. My booking data shows specialist rooms sitting idle, while general spaces are always full. We’re paying for the wrong things.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,George,,"@Yumi, that confirms my fear. We are paying for empty specialist rooms while general spaces overflow, and our staff are stuck doing manual work.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Mizuki,,"@Yumi, exactly. My delivery data confirms it: comfort-based projects slip, yet we keep choosing them. We need to prioritize what actually gets used.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Mizuki, precisely. We keep chasing comfort while the market inflates and our reserves stay empty. The math simply doesn’t work.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Shizue,,"I’m glad we’re seeing the same picture. The rain is real, but the rising costs are the true thief. Let’s hope the candidates reflect this reality.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Yumi,,I’m relieved the data backs up my gut feeling. We need to stop building empty boxes and start fixing what’s actually broken.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,George,,"- **George**: Agreed. We must stop ignoring the human cost. If we pick a project that demands more manual labor, we are setting ourselves up for failure.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Mizuki,,"Agreed. The data is clear: we must choose a project that delivers immediate, measurable value to the whole campus, not just a single department.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""name_label"",""name"":""Mizuki"",""self"":true,""raw"":""Mizuki: Agreed. The data is clear: we must choose a project that delivers immediate, measurable value to the whole campus, not just a single department.""}]}"
54,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,Agreed. We must stop funding vanity projects with borrowed money. Let’s see which candidate actually respects the market and our empty reserves.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
