60,3,1,talk,Shizue,,The candidates are here. I’m looking for one that won’t get stuck in the rain or the budget.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Yumi,,"- **Yumi**: @Shizue, I’m hoping one of these actually fixes the overcrowding in our general rooms instead of adding more empty specialist spaces.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,George,,"@Yumi, I’m watching for any plan that forces my exhausted staff into more manual routines. We simply cannot absorb another burden.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Mizuki,,"@George, I’m looking for a project with broad, open access. My data shows that’s the only way to guarantee high usage and avoid disappointment.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"@Mizuki, broad access is fine, but I’m watching for hidden maintenance costs. I refuse to fund a project that quietly drains our empty reserves.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Shizue,,"- **Shizue**: @Benjamin, I worry about A. Outdoor work invites the rain, and my diaries show how many weeks that steals from us.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Yumi,,"@Shizue, I worry about D. My data shows general rooms are always full, so C fixes the real problem without adding empty specialist spaces.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,George,,"@Yumi, C is safer for my staff, but D’s ventilation failure is forcing my technicians into dangerous manual labor. We must fix that.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@George, I understand the urgency, but my data shows single-wing benefits get the lowest ratings. C offers open access to everyone, which guarantees the usage we need.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@George, D is a trap. My reserve data proves we cannot afford the ongoing maintenance of complex plant. C is the only fiscally responsible choice.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Shizue,,"@Benjamin, I agree. C is indoors, so the rain cannot steal our weeks. It is the only plan that respects both the weather and our empty pockets.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Yumi,,"@Shizue, exactly. C solves the overcrowding I see in the booking data. It’s the only option that actually serves the people who need space most.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,George,,"- **George**: @Benjamin, I concede C is safer for my staff, but D’s ventilation failure is forcing my technicians into dangerous manual labor. We must fix that.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Mizuki,,"@George, I hear your urgency, but my data shows single-wing projects disappoint. C serves the whole campus, which is where the real value lies.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
